# `result/` is PUBLISHED, not ignored (owner's ruling, 2026-09-27, revised).
#
# One subfolder per request under `result/`, never a sibling `out-<name>/` at the skill
# root - that rule is unchanged, and it is what makes `result/` safe to publish: a run's
# artifacts are all in one reviewable place instead of scattered at the skill root.
#
# Why it is now tracked: the run folders ARE the public evidence of what the skill
# produces - `report.md`, the PNGs, `series.csv`, `metrics.json`, the optional
# `report.pdf`. A visitor reads them in place. Two subfolders currently live here and
# both are publishable as-is: `ai-uk-en/` (a real run) and the run-independent docs
# `desc.md`, `manual.md`, `result.md` (the description, the user manual, the results
# write-up - all referenced by README.md).
#
# `out/` stays ignored: it is the scratch default of the `--out` flag for a bare
# `scripts/build_report.py` invocation, so whatever sits there is a throwaway rerun, not
# a curated artifact.
#
# The gate moved with the ruling:
# `tests/test_publish.py::test_result_is_published_not_ignored` asserts there is NO
# `result` rule here, and that a run folder is actually TRACKED - because a stale rule
# left over from the earlier ruling would silently unpublish all of it.

# The owner's private simulation-test record, kept on disk and never published.
#
# bug.md and test.md are the 2026-09-27 free-model test report and the five
# defects it found. They are the source of truth Phase 8 worked from and are
# cited by .planning/, but they are an internal working record rather than part
# of the skill:
#   * test.md line 35 carries a REAL personal email address in a
#     WTI_USER_AGENT example, and this repository is public;
#   * both files name a real person and a real model identifier for the run.
# The five findings themselves are not secret - they are all fixed, all fixed in
# code, and all covered by committed regressions - so the repository loses
# nothing by excluding the two reports. `git rm --cached` was used, not a
# delete: both files remain on disk and remain the reference for the Phase 8
# verification.
bug.md
test.md
